      "value": "Additional report: same crash bucket, 4 users, one world, one evening\n\nWe run a weekly group event in our world and hit this crash on multiple PCs during our first large event on the Unity 6 client.\n\nWorld: The Bar EXODUST, group+ instance, capacity 40\n\nClient: 2026.3.3p2-1921-15c4a824b2 (Unity 6000.0.67f1-DWR)\n\nDate: 2026-10-25 22:30–25:00 JST\n\nCrash signature (Windows Reliability Monitor), identical on all checked PCs:\n\n- UnityPlayer.dll 6000.0.67.6863, exception c0000005, offset 0x0000000000b11b2d\n\n- Bucket ID: 766c1fa51efc85364d935189e381e1a7\n\nAffected users (all different machines):\n\n- User A: i9-13900F / RTX 4070 Ti / 64 GB / Desktop (crashed 4 times in one evening)\n\n- User B: i9-13900F / RTX 4080 / 64 GB / Desktop\n\n- User C: Ryzen 7 5700X / RTX 3080 Ti / 32 GB / VR (Quest 3 via Virtual Desktop)\n\n- User D: separate PC, same bucket ID confirmed\n\nPattern in output_log (same on every crash):\n\n1. Join an instance with roughly 16–30 players\n\n2. Many \"Avatar is Ready, Initializing\" lines in the same second\n\n3. \"Waiting for players to network ready\"\n\n4. \"[TextureManagement] Over cache size but failed to find any textures to remove\" (several times)\n\n5. \"Initialize Limb Avatar VRCPlayer[Remote] N False 1\" for several remote players\n\n6. The log ends and the client closes. No managed exception is logged.\n\nTime from join to crash: about 8–12 seconds. Retrying sometimes succeeds.\n\nUsers who had avatar display limits off (Safety Level: None) seemed to be affected more.\n\nTimeline:\n\n- 2026-09-27: event with a similar crowd size on the pre-Unity 6 client, no crashes\n\n- 2026-10-25: first large event on 2026.3.3p2, repeated crashes during joins\n\n- We made only a trivial world change in between (two TextMeshPro labels). We removed it and reviewed the world, and found nothing related on the world side.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
